    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="1029" n="985" xml:id="pg985"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 336</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, Prepared in the Department
                        of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d541-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" type="conversation-or-meeting-date"
                            when="1954-06-27">June 27, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>Participants:</label>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States</hi>
                        <list>
                            <item>The Secretary</item>
                            <item>Mr. Merchant </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United Kingdom</hi>
                        <list>
                            <item>Mr. Anthony Eden </item>
                            <item> Sir Harold Caccia </item>
                            <item> Christopher Soames </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <list rendition="#flush" subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Germany and E.D.C. </item>
                </list>
                <p>At noon today while waiting to join the President and Prime Minister, there was a
                    considerable discussion of the problem of Germany. The Secretary and Mr. Eden
                    agreed that their estimates coincided on the importance of taking positive
                    action in support of Adenauer if the French Assembly recessed this summer
                    without ratifying EDC. They were in general agreement that a way should be found
                    to separate the contractuals from the EDC, without prejudice to possible later
                    action by the French Assembly in approving EDC in the fall. This would require
                    some undertaking from Adenauer that Germany would not unilaterally rearm during
                    the period in which the fate of EDC would be settled. The Secretary explained
                    the constitutional requirements with which we were faced in connection with
                    modifying the Bonn Treaty so as to remove the link with the EDC Treaty. Mr. Eden
                    was obviously unaware of this complication but recognized it when it was pointed
                    out. There was agreement that Adenauer should be consulted before any approach
                    to the French.</p>
            </div>
